Decide sooner that the capture has no echo when the sound plays to headphones and nothing shows an echo path

With a headset and the far end talking from the start of a call, AEC3 has no echo path to
learn and takes the strong render for echo it cannot yet cancel: the near voice comes out
suppressed by more than 6 dB for about 5 s, the last loss near 7.5 s, until the legacy
transparent mode (5 s without a sane filter, 6 s of strong render) takes the capture for a
headset's. Measured in the AEC3 simulator (M158 with main's patches and 0017, 16 kHz,
far speech or music, near speech, room noise at -76 and -52 dBFS).

Waiting less for everyone lets echo through on speakers: 3 s instead of 5 and 6 passes
quiet music's echo (-30 dB, 300 ms) in the seconds between two changes of its delay, up to
18 dB more in one half second. Within AEC3 alone, the start of a call with a headset and
near speech cannot be told from double talk from the start over a weak echo (-20 to -30
dB) whose delay is not yet found: the same filter convergence, no delay, and a bound on
the echo path's gain that room noise raises to about -35 dB.

So the audio device module now says whether the sound plays to headphones or a headset
(PlayoutToHeadphones, next to the count of patch 0011), and the legacy transparent mode
waits 3 s instead of 5 and 6 only while it does and nothing shows an echo path: no delay
found for the echo since the last reset, the filters converged in no more than 25 blocks,
and the least ratio of the capture to the render a lag before, over 4 blocks, below -35 dB
at every lag up to 512 ms. A delay found, more convergence or a larger ratio keep the usual
wait. The mode logs when it turns on or off.

Simulator: with the sound to headphones, the near voice is suppressed 2.0 s instead of 5.0
(last loss at 3.5 s, not 7.5), also with room noise at -52 dBFS; with a quiet far end 0.5
to 1.5 s instead of 2 to 4.5. Without it everything is identical: the start of a call with
music or speech on speakers or a headset, quiet music, double talk from the start, echo of
5 to 30 ms with 0017, echo that appears 2 to 7 s into the call, the unmute series. With it
and an echo (headphones that leak, or speakers named as headphones): echo of -25 to -40 dB
is identical, -45 and -50 dB 2 to 5 dB more in one half second where it already passed;
double talk from the start with music at -30 dB and 200 ms lets the echo through from 2.5
s instead of 3 in one of two seeds.

